orld Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133096534,imgsize-126868.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why did Kick streamer TreyLiving slap Fishtank contestant Burt Bronx on camera? Here’s what we know]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133095083.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[During a livestream event, tensions flared when TreyLiving and Burt Bronx got into a physical altercation. While Trey was shirtless, Burt reportedly slapped him on the butt, prompting an enraged reaction from Trey, who retaliated with multiple slaps to Burt. This unexpected incident has ignited a wave of discussions online about appropriate conduct and consent in streaming environments, with the footage rapidly gaining traction across social media platforms.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-did-kick-streamer-treyliving-slap-fishtank-contestant-burt-bronx-on-camera-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133095083.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-did-kick-streamer-treyliving-slap-fishtank-contestant-burt-bronx-on-camera-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/133095083.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T15:24:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133095218,imgsize-867940.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[British national killed in PoK clashes; another held for over 2 months: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133095197.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/british-national-killed-in-pok-clashes-another-held-for-over-2-months-report/articleshow/133095197.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/british-national-killed-in-pok-clashes-another-held-for-over-2-months-report/articleshow/133095197.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T15:31:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133095324,imgsize-176534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lake Mead's falling water levels are revealing a US ghost town submerged by its waters 90 years ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133094037.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The receding waters of Lake Mead have unveiled the eerie remnants of St. Thomas, a ghost town in Nevada. Originally a thriving Mormon settlement founded in 1865, it was swallowed by rising waters after the Hoover Dam was built in 1938. Now, the lakebed displays its foundations, allowing history enthusiasts a rare opportunity to connect with a bygone era of agricultural significance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hoover-dams-construction-submerged-a-us-town-in-1935-90-years-later-lake-meads-falling-water-levels-are-helping-it-reemerge/articleshow/133094037.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hoover-dams-construction-submerged-a-us-town-in-1935-90-years-later-lake-meads-falling-water-levels-are-helping-it-reemerge/articleshow/133094037.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133094356,imgsize-126722.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[German scientists made a sponge-like material that pulls drinking water from air]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133092453.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/german-scientists-made-a-sponge-like-material-that-pulls-drinking-water-from-air-as-dry-as-18-humidity-producing-up-to-1-8-litres-per-kg-each-day/articleshow/133092453.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/german-scientists-made-a-sponge-like-material-that-pulls-drinking-water-from-air-as-dry-as-18-humidity-producing-up-to-1-8-litres-per-kg-each-day/articleshow/133092453.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T14:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133093793,imgsize-139604.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[3,500-year-old residential complex discovered in Egypt]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133090751.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/3500-year-old-residential-complex-discovered-in-egypt-with-connections-dating-back-to-the-bible-era/articleshow/133090751.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/3500-year-old-residential-complex-discovered-in-egypt-with-connections-dating-back-to-the-bible-era/articleshow/133090751.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T13:32:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133090751,imgsize-223372.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Two people bitten by beavers in less than two weeks at Maryland park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133092056.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At Cunningham Falls State Park, two people experienced beaver bites that resulted in positive rabies tests for both animals involved. Consequently, park authorities have restricted access to water areas to ensure public safety. Ongoing surveillance is focused on assessing the rabies situation, and restrictions will persist until health officials confirm that the park is safe for all visitors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-people-bitten-by-beavers-in-less-than-two-weeks-at-maryland-park-force-partial-closure-after-both-animals-test-positive-for-rabies/articleshow/133092056.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-people-bitten-by-beavers-in-less-than-two-weeks-at-maryland-park-force-partial-closure-after-both-animals-test-positive-for-rabies/articleshow/133092056.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T14:00:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133092056,imgsize-2518424.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China’s first freshwater cave snail in a dark mountain cave]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133092024.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-chinas-first-freshwater-cave-snail-in-a-dark-mountain-cave-but-only-three-living-adults-have-been-found/articleshow/133092024.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-chinas-first-freshwater-cave-snail-in-a-dark-mountain-cave-but-only-three-living-adults-have-been-found/articleshow/133092024.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T13:51:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133092120,imgsize-52640.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Singapore replaced a 2.7-km concrete canal with a winding river; biodiversity rose 30%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133088519.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Singapore transformed a 2.7-km concrete canal at Bishan-Ang Mo Kio Park into a 3-km meandering river between 2009 and 2011. The project created a flood plain and more varied river habitat. Later research found 26 fish species in the rehabilitated section, including three native species, compared with eight non-native species in an untreated canal section.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2012-singapore-replaced-a-2-7-km-concrete-drainage-channel-with-a-3-km-winding-river-biodiversity-in-the-park-increased-by-30/articleshow/133088519.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2012-singapore-replaced-a-2-7-km-concrete-drainage-channel-with-a-3-km-winding-river-biodiversity-in-the-park-increased-by-30/articleshow/133088519.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T13:52:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133090353,imgsize-212778.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida community fears radioactive waste pile could threaten many living nearby]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133069230.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Residents of Progress Village are increasingly concerned about the environmental and health threats posed by a substantial phosphogypsum stack nearby. This waste contains naturally occurring radioactive materials, raising alarms about radiation exposure and potential water contamination, particularly during storm events. Studies on the stack's effects on local air and water quality have been conducted, and the community is advocating for greater transparency and improved management of this hazardous industrial waste.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-community-fears-a-radioactive-waste-pile-could-threaten-thousands-living-nearby/articleshow/133069230.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-community-fears-a-radioactive-waste-pile-could-threaten-thousands-living-nearby/articleshow/133069230.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T22:21:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133069230,imgsize-1091700.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[French winemaker spent €4 million on 6,000 solar panels to protect grapes ]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133087691.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/a-french-winemaker-spent-4-million-on-6000-solar-panels-to-protect-grapes-from-heat-and-hail-but-lost-the-official-cognac-label/articleshow/133087691.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/a-french-winemaker-spent-4-million-on-6000-solar-panels-to-protect-grapes-from-heat-and-hail-but-lost-the-official-cognac-label/articleshow/133087691.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T11:57:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133087825,imgsize-349302.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US mosquito numbers have crashed during a historic drought]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133088108.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mosquito-numbers-have-crashed-during-a-historic-drought-but-scientists-say-fewer-mosquitoes-can-still-mean-a-higher-risk-of-west-nile-virus/articleshow/133088108.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-mosquito-numbers-have-crashed-during-a-historic-drought-but-scientists-say-fewer-mosquitoes-can-still-mean-a-higher-risk-of-west-nile-virus/articleshow/133088108.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T12:15:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133088339,imgsize-3096479.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In the 1990s, Boston sent Big Dig soil to a burning dump, turning it into a park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133087173.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Boston’s massive Big Dig project produced more than 16 million cubic yards of soil, and nearly a quarter of it was sent to Spectacle Island in Boston Harbor. The island was once a city dump where methane gas caused underground fires. The soil helped cap the old landfill, reshape the island and support a long restoration effort that brought back trees, plants, birds and other wildlife.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1990s-boston-sent-nearly-a-quarter-of-the-big-digs-16-million-cubic-yards-of-soil-to-a-burning-former-dump-island-and-helped-turn-it-into-a-park/articleshow/133087173.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1990s-boston-sent-nearly-a-quarter-of-the-big-digs-16-million-cubic-yards-of-soil-to-a-burning-former-dump-island-and-helped-turn-it-into-a-park/articleshow/133087173.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T12:57:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133087762,imgsize-150656.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gujarat canal-top solar generates power while saving 2.38M gallons of water]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133088197.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Gujarat, India, a groundbreaking solar plant is ingeniously situated over an irrigation canal, generating electricity while simultaneously conserving water. By minimizing evaporation and discouraging algae growth, this project exemplifies the efficient use of existing infrastructure for multiple benefits. Given Gujarat's vast canal system, this innovative model showcases a promising solution to tackle land scarcity while enhancing water management.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-half-mile-solar-strip-floats-above-an-irrigation-canal-in-gujarat-generating-1-6-million-kilowatt-hours-of-power-while-saving-2-38-million-gallons-of-water-from-evaporation/articleshow/133088197.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-half-mile-solar-strip-floats-above-an-irrigation-canal-in-gujarat-generating-1-6-million-kilowatt-hours-of-power-while-saving-2-38-million-gallons-of-water-from-evaporation/articleshow/133088197.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T12:57:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133088658,imgsize-133769.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Melinda French Gates: "When something's uncomfortable, it means you're actually…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133089551.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-melinda-french-gates-when-somethings-uncomfortable-it-means-youre-actually-a-lesson-on-stepping-outside-your-comfort-zone/articleshow/133089551.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-melinda-french-gates-when-somethings-uncomfortable-it-means-youre-actually-a-lesson-on-stepping-outside-your-comfort-zone/articleshow/133089551.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T12:48:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133089551,imgsize-1782767.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Japan’s ‘women of the sea’: 80-year-old diver dives into cold waters without an oxygen tank]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133088629.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Ama of Japan, elite free divers who have harvested seafood without oxygen tanks for centuries, face a critical moment in their history. With an aging population of divers and the changing dynamics of ocean ecosystems, this age-old fishing tradition is at risk. Local communities are banding together to protect and celebrate this unparalleled cultural legacy, ensuring that the spirit of the Ama continues to thrive amidst adversity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-japans-women-of-the-sea-80-year-old-diver-dives-into-cold-waters-without-an-oxygen-tank-to-harvest-seafood-using-a-centuries-old-tradition/articleshow/133088629.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-japans-women-of-the-sea-80-